# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true here) checks every text file
# out with CRLF, while prettier's own rule is LF. The two disagree silently and
# the result is a file that fails `prettier --check` the moment git rewrites it
# -- a `git checkout`, a stash pop, a branch switch -- with an empty `git diff`,
# because git normalizes the line endings back out again when it compares. That
# combination cost real debugging time twice: once on docs/prd.md, and once
# during a stash probe in the stage 5 work.
#
# LF in the working tree is safe for this toolchain. Node, prettier, eslint,
# vitest and expo all read LF natively on Windows, and every editor in use here
# writes it back unchanged.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files git must never touch. Fonts and images have no line endings, and
# a well-meaning conversion inside one corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.m4a binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
